{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>Goyim</b> Written גיים — allusion to the ten nations that came to destroy the Temple: the tents of Edom and the Ishmaelites, etc., and they are יו״ד. Another interpretation: גיים = 63; this one was blessed with a son of 63, and this one came with 63 nations in the destruction of the Second Temple, for 7 nations were uprooted. And that is what is written: הכל ס״ג יחדו נאלחו." "<b>Two nations in your womb</b> — in gematria this is Rabbi Yehudah and Antoninus." "<b>And the one nation over the other nation shall prevail</b> — shall overpower its fellow and destroy it. And that is what is written: אמלאה החרבה."], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {0 "The phrase הכל ס״ג יחדו נאלחו appears to be a citation of a phrase whose source is uncertain; translated hyper-literally as 'all 63 together they were joined.'"}, :source-witnesses [["Kitzur Baal HaTurim" "http://sefaria.org"] ["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:16:58.104563601Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}